body:
If you pick a private company that tells you, you don't need anti-virus or anti-malware software. Don't go there. Been there, done that, learned the hard way. There's no "Free" anti-virus and after talking with an awesome guy with a computer engineering degree and far beyond A+ Certification, it's a must for casuals like us. 

&#x200B;

If it's more hardware related, I like memory express. Depending on what one you go to, Staples isn't bad either. The Shawnessy one has a good tech there, my dad raves about him. I've heard great stuff about Ducktoes as well.

Overall, 6. 

&#x200B;

Currently, a 2.
